aarch64 build of https://github.com/xXJSONDeruloXx/lsfg-vk tag fp16-test-2 (the
fork decky-lsfg-vk 0.12.2 pins), built natively on the device with clang:
  python3 liblsfg-vk-arm64.patch.py            # skip Wine helper processes
  python3 liblsfg-vk-arm64.dispatch-patch.py   # per-chain dispatch, swapchain-only hooking
  cmake -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang \
        -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang++ -DCMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS="-Wl,-z,nodelete"
  ninja -C build
Why: the plugin only ships an x86-64 liblsfg-vk.so (skipped by the arm64 loader).
Upstream kept next-layer proc addrs in globals; in Proton ARM64 Wine's explorer.exe
that routed a device into MangoHud's GetDeviceProcAddr from another chain -> NULL
deref -> winex11.drv init failure -> SIGSEGV loop, games stuck "launching".
Layer manifest: /usr/share/vulkan/implicit_layer.d/VkLayer_LS_frame_generation_arm64.json
(enabled only when LSFG_PROCESS=decky-lsfg-vk, which ~/lsfg exports).
Verified 2026-09-24: Dying Light (Proton 11 ARM64) runs with frame generation.
